## Scope of the Harish Code changes

Harish Code does **not** reimplement the application. The changes in this
repository are presentational and identity-related only:

1. **Product identity** — window title, application name, menu labels, user
   agent, executable metadata (`ProductName`, `FileDescription`,
   `CompanyName`) and update channel are set to *Harish Code*.
2. **Artwork** — a new HC monogram replaces every OpenCode mark in the UI:
   the home screen wordmark, the provider avatar, the About wordmark and the
   decorative brush artwork. In-app marks are inline SVG using
   `currentColor`, so they adapt to light and dark themes.
3. **Copy** — user-facing strings across all locale bundles and the About
   page are rebranded. Credits point to
   [@harishpixous-commits](https://github.com/harishpixous-commits).
4. **Application icons** — the embedded executable icon, window icons,
   favicons and tiles are all generated from the HC artwork.

## What was deliberately *not* changed

Some occurrences of the string `OpenCode` remain on purpose, because renaming
them breaks the application:

- the internal RPC namespace export (`OpenCode:()=>…`) and its consumers
- provider identifiers (`opencode`, `opencode-go`)
- storage keys (`opencode.global.dat`, `opencode.window`, `opencode.draft.*`)
- log paths and the `@opencode/client` package import paths

Third-party service names shown in *Settings → Providers* (for example
**OpenCode Go** and **OpenCode Console**) also remain: those are real external
products, listed alongside Anthropic, OpenAI and Google, and renaming them
would misrepresent someone else's service.

